Intercom existing Agency session connector qualification

Workstream ID: ic-04
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/3
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Proven capability for the actual existing Agency session
Dependencies: ic-01

Purpose:
  Validate the essential integration before building a voice/desktop shell
  around an assumed API. The owner now authorizes one designated existing
  idle-session conversation and subsequently confirmed background work,
  retaining manual approvals and refusing busy writers. Active attach is excluded.

Tasks:
  [x] Qualify exact Agency discovery and bounded existing-session conversation.
  [x] Verify installed ACP existing-session load and explicit manual policy.
  [x] Exercise one approved read-only tool with actual terminal response/speech.
  [ ] Qualify actual native permission requests without retained saved grants.
  [ ] Obtain further authority/disposable workspaces for the broader capability tests.
  [ ] Discover sessions with source/capability/active-state distinctions.
  [ ] Qualify active attach and dormant resume separately; preserve launch policy.
  [ ] Validate effective resumed permission state and ACP versus SDK transport.
  [ ] Prove request identity, structured events, approvals and terminal handoff.
  [ ] Exercise failure, busy state, cancellation and uncertain dispatch.
  [ ] Record a versioned capability receipt and feed findings into ic-02.

Acceptance criteria:
  The target is an existing Agency session, not a silently substituted SDK session.
  Same identity/workspace and relevant configuration are verified.
  Inherited allow-all/unknown policy cannot bypass host confirmation guarantees.
  Unsupported active attachment is an explicit limitation, not a successful proof.
  One dispatch yields attributable events/outcome without agent-prompt polling.
  No competing writer, blanket permission grant or unapproved service activation.
  Human approval and technical qualification remain distinct.

Completion evidence:
  Actual Agency catalog distinguishes resumable copilot_cli, idle and in_use.
  The designated existing session returned "Hello world." through direct
  Copilot resume, with successful task_complete, exact terminal session ID and
  result/process exit zero. No new session or competing writer was created.
  The packaged integrated voice smoke also returns an ordinary "Hello world."
  assistant reply, persisted only after the matching successful final result.
  Ordinary conversation need not invoke task_complete. An observed initial
  parser failure was investigated in existing session history before any retry;
  accepting plain replies preserves exact terminal correlation and rejects
  explicit failed tasks. Nine host/native cases cover these boundaries.
  Current transport exposes only task_complete, denies shell/write, disables
  built-in MCPs/custom instructions and never grants blanket approval.
  Host tests reject missing/browse-only/in-use identities, unexpected tools,
  mismatched/failed completion and duplicate work; native owned-child
  cancellation is exercised. This is not active attach, ACP/SDK parity,
  inherited permission audit, arbitrary tool work or terminal-handoff proof.
  See docs/architecture/architecture.md and docs/product/roadmap.md for the proposed proof boundary.
  docs/architecture/runtime-contracts.md expands the capability/ownership and dispatch rules.
  The current ACP path explicitly sets/verifies Agent mode then allow-all OFF,
  retains the inherited model and applies supported profile reasoning effort.
  One separately approved native source test ran only Get-Location and returned
  "Hello world." with completed local playback, exact existing identity and
  observed successful tool event. Existing saved grants covered the operation;
  no native permission prompt occurred. Fixtures cover exact one-shot allow/
  reject, policy/session identity, stream failures and cancellation boundaries.
  Session catalogs remain bounded to 2,000 rows over at most four 500-row pages;
  per-page native rebuild cost motivated avoiding redundant small pages.
  A new terminal opens for manual task entry only, not automatic ownership
  transfer or monitored completion. Broader connector criteria remain open.

Completion log:
